WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.102
On-site assessment compares the forecast with actual conditions at the place and time of flight.

00:00:07.102 --> 00:00:14.205
Record wind direction, average behavior, gusts, temperature, visibility, precipitation, clouds, sun, and signs of change.

00:00:14.205 --> 00:00:16.572
Observe terrain and structures.

00:00:16.572 --> 00:00:23.245
Flags, trees, water, dust, smoke, drifting precipitation, and cloud movement can reveal local effects.

00:00:23.245 --> 00:00:29.486
A sheltered staging area may hide the wind or turbulence along the route.

00:00:29.486 --> 00:00:37.450
Inspect launch and recovery surfaces for water, snow, ice, dust, loose debris, mud, slope, and crew footing.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:45.413
Confirm emergency landing areas remain available and that people, vehicles, or activity have not changed the plan.

00:00:45.413 --> 00:00:53.376
Brief the crew on current conditions, thresholds, route, battery reserve, communication terms, landing options, and abort criteria.

00:00:53.376 --> 00:01:00.479
Everyone should understand that raising a concern is expected, not an obstacle to mission completion.

00:01:00.479 --> 00:01:03.707
Conditions must be monitored during flight.

00:01:03.707 --> 00:01:10.810
Watch aircraft attitude, groundspeed, battery use, signal, image quality, precipitation, visibility, and changing ground activity.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:14.469
Trends matter before an alert becomes critical.

00:01:14.469 --> 00:01:19.849
If actual conditions differ materially from the plan, pause and reassess.

00:01:19.849 --> 00:01:26.091
A decision made at the office does not obligate the crew to launch.

00:01:26.091 --> 00:01:31.041
Record the final go, delay, modification, or cancellation and why.

00:01:31.041 --> 00:01:38.144
Client schedules, travel cost, expiring access, or a waiting crew can create pressure to continue.

00:01:38.144 --> 00:01:45.676
Predefined criteria give the pilot a defensible basis for saying no before that pressure narrows judgment.
